# Sources of the bootstrap-language study (hub 4.1). Web pages reached the study through a summarising fetch tool.

n: 2.11
name: bootstrap-language-sources
kind: hub
is: Sources of the bootstrap-language study of 2026-11-24: the study report, the first-round critic's review, one old-body file, and 40 public pages on Apple's JIT rules, Windows and Linux executable memory, Go, Rust, C code generators, Zig and bootstrappable builds. Every page was read through a fetch tool that summarises.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/web-bootstrap-language

n: 2.11.1
name: web-bootstrap-language.md
kind: source
is: The study report on the bootstrap language: C, Go and Rust compared, with Zig and hex or assembly as outside options, 516 lines. It holds the experiments run on one Apple M4 Max under macOS 26.3.1 and the list of pages fetched.
path: coherence-seed/study/r1/web-bootstrap-language.md
date: 2026-11-24
got: 2026-11-24
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/web-bootstrap-language

n: 2.11.2
name: critic.md
kind: source
is: The completeness critique of the first study round, 472 lines: gaps, 47 spot-checks with verdicts, contradictions between reports, and what is ready to decide.
path: coherence-seed/study/r1/critic.md
date: 2026-11-24
got: 2026-11-24
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/web-bootstrap-language

